WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.940
Telepathic dogs, eerily topical pandemics,
mass infertility.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:10.972
When it comes to zombies, disease, or mass
extinction, these films are the cream of the crop.

00:00:10.972 --> 00:00:16.285
Apocalyptic films are teeming with the walking
dead, nuclear threats, and catastrophic plagues.

00:00:16.285 --> 00:00:21.911
But only one film on this list sees the world
sizzle to a crisp thanks to dragons.

00:00:21.911 --> 00:00:27.670
Set in the totally-not-apocalyptic year of
2020, where dragons have replaced mankind

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:32.989
as the dominant species, the paltry remnants
of the human race must work together to ensure

00:00:32.989 --> 00:00:34.110
their survival.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:41.050
Maligned upon its release and criminally under-seen,
Reign of Fire is much more interesting, visually

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:44.570
stunning, and sophisticated than its goofy
premise suggests.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:50.900
With an all-star cast and some genuinely jaw-dropping
creature effects, it's a must-watch for anyone

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:52.390
who wants to see the world burn.

00:00:53.125 --> 00:00:57.829
This loose adaptation of Richard Matheson's
classic novel follows scientist Robert Neville

00:00:57.829 --> 00:01:02.079
who is, as far as he can tell, one of the
last human beings on Earth.

00:01:02.079 --> 00:01:06.920
Thanks to an attempt to cure cancer that mutated
into a deadly virus, most humans have become

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.200
pallid, vampiric creatures.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:14.299
Balancing mind-numbing loneliness with his
attempts to survive and develop a cure, Neville

00:01:14.299 --> 00:01:18.450
soon finds that he is far less alone than
he initially suspected.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:22.759
Grounded by a heartfelt performance by Will
Smith and featuring more action than the vast

00:01:22.759 --> 00:01:29.940
majority of films on this list, I Am Legend
is a punchy, big-budget take on an apocalyptic ur-text.

00:01:30.505 --> 00:01:32.359
"Please say 'Hello,' to me."

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:39.340
This film tells of a uniquely terrifying plague,
which only attacks strains of grasses and

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.190
grains, including wheat and rice.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:46.159
In the wake of this catastrophe, the world
descends into famine, and, consequently, chaos.

00:01:46.159 --> 00:01:50.710
We follow an upper-middle class architect
named John, who becomes the de facto patriarch

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:54.890
of a group of family, friends, and stragglers
as they make their way to the safe haven of

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:56.100
his brother's farm.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:02:00.780
Pay no attention to the film's middling Rotten
Tomatoes score: What No Blade of Grass lacks

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:08.020
in polish and a finer touch it more than makes
up for in grim, stifling ecological terror.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:13.280
Enduringly relevant and dystopian, No Blade
of Grass is an essential watch for anyone

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:17.910
with a taste for the dreary, hopeless outlook
of 1970s science fiction.

00:02:18.483 --> 00:02:23.605
Ralph Burton is a miner who is trapped underground
while a nuclear holocaust wipes out all of humanity.

00:02:23.605 --> 00:02:28.890
Emerging to find New York City deserted, Ralph
assumes he's the last man on Earth, and starts

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:29.681
acting like it.

00:02:29.681 --> 00:02:32.980
Eventually, Ralph meets Sarah, a fellow survivor.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:37.370
However, their dynamic is soon disturbed by
the arrival of another survivor.

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:42.270
Starring the trailblazing screen star and
activist Harry Belafonte, The World, the Flesh,

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:47.420
and the Devil feels like a lost Twilight Zone
episode filtered through the lens of Richard Matheson.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:53.000
Tackling its societal themes head-on and highlighting
Belafonte's undeniable screen presence, this

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:58.709
film is an unmissable and decidedly more optimistic
entry in apocalyptic cinema.

00:02:58.986 --> 00:03:04.530
Sunshine dramatizes a horrific, world-ending
scenario: The sun is dying.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:09.390
As the planet Earth is thrust into colder
and colder temperatures, a team of crack astronauts

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:14.390
are sent to kick-start the all-important star
by firing a nuclear bomb into its core.

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:19.640
Full of incredible visuals and shocking horror
beats, particularly in the third act, Sunshine

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:24.519
is an enthralling and atmospheric slice of
science fiction with stakes that don't just

00:03:24.519 --> 00:03:27.200
threaten humanity, but our whole solar system.

00:03:27.666 --> 00:03:33.299
This sci-fi survival horror film and Cloverfield
sequel follows Michelle, a young woman who

00:03:33.299 --> 00:03:37.750
wakes up in an underground bunker after a
violent roadside accident.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:42.299
Unsettled by her domineering captor, Howard,
who claims the air outside is toxic and she

00:03:42.299 --> 00:03:47.718
cannot leave under any circumstances, resourceful
Michelle sets about plotting her escape.

00:03:47.718 --> 00:03:49.270
"Please, just let me go.

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:49.893
Please."

00:03:49.893 --> 00:03:52.081
"There is nowhere to go, Michelle."

00:03:52.081 --> 00:03:59.750
This economically paced and wildly tense single-location
thriller boasts numerous top-shelf performances

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:02.129
and a claustrophobic sense of unease.

00:04:02.129 --> 00:04:08.492
If the world ended and you were trapped underground
with an overbearing psycho, what would you do?

00:04:08.492 --> 00:04:14.417
From its title, you'd be forgiven for mistaking
this film for some kind of adorable sea-side romantic comedy.

00:04:14.417 --> 00:04:19.850
It is, in fact, about an atomic war that wipes
out all organic life in the Northern Hemisphere.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:24.540
A surviving yankee submarine finds respite
in Australia, which appears to be one of the

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:26.540
few safe harbors on Earth.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:32.110
Where many films on this list veer into action
or hard sci-fi territory, On the Beach opts

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:33.110
for melodrama.

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:36.729
Sure, there's still plenty of nihilism and
social commentary, but on the whole, it feels

00:04:36.729 --> 00:04:41.000
much more like an existential soap opera than
an explosion-heavy thriller.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:46.638
On the Beach pulls this off by featuring a
powerful ensemble cast full of big-name talent.

00:04:46.781 --> 00:04:52.270
Adapted from the 1962 French film La Jetée,
12 Monkeys follows James Cole, a convict from

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:56.960
the year 2035 sent through time to find a
solution to the world's dark fate.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:02.900
In 1996, a deadly virus of unknown origin
eradicated almost all life on Earth, forcing

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.030
those who survived underground.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:09.449
The plan is to send Cole back to the day of
the outbreak to learn how it all went down.

00:05:09.449 --> 00:05:13.910
But when he's accidentally transported too
far back, his warnings of the end of days

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:15.970
land him in a mental hospital.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:22.389
Boasting evocative production design and expectation-subverting
performances from its two male leads, 12 Monkeys

00:05:22.389 --> 00:05:27.570
is a frantic, doom-filled ride with both style
and substance.

00:05:27.686 --> 00:05:32.548
A Boy and His Dog takes place in the barren,
irradiated wastes of 2024.

00:05:32.548 --> 00:05:38.160
Our hero is Vic, a morally suspect teenage
boy who wanders from one bombed-out hole in

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:41.300
the ground to the next in search of food and
women.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:45.773
Along for the ride is Blood, a telepathic
dog full of wry commentary.

00:05:45.988 --> 00:05:47.808
"Charity is a thing of the past."

00:05:47.808 --> 00:05:54.021
This film is bleak, perverse, and offbeat
— aka, the holy trinity of 1970s apocalyptic

00:05:54.021 --> 00:05:55.021
science fiction.

00:05:55.406 --> 00:06:00.449
If you shook your fists at those who held
super-spreader house parties during the COVID-19

00:06:00.449 --> 00:06:03.380
pandemic, boy have we got the film for you!

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:08.660
A top-shelf product of Roger Corman and Vincent
Price's yen for Edgar Allan Poe adaptations,

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:13.720
The Masque of the Red Death follows Prince
Prospero, a hedonistic Satanist who has resolved

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:19.000
to lock himself and his party guests in his
enormous castle to stave off the terrible

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.440
plague known as the Red Death.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:27.440
Full of cruelty, scene-chewing, and gorgeous
production design realized in jaw-dropping

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:32.810
Technicolor, The Masque of the Red Death is
a lavish visual feast of gothic delights that

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:38.873
overcomes its budgetary limitations to deliver
one of the most striking products of Corman's career.

00:06:38.873 --> 00:06:44.400
When animal rights activists unwittingly release
a rabies-like virus onto the British public,

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:47.660
the country is catapulted back to the Dark
Ages.

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:52.280
Four weeks later, a man named Jim wakes from
a coma and surveys the wreckage of what used

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:53.590
to be London.

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:58.270
Rescued by a group of survivors, Jim finds
that infected humans now stalk the streets,

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:01.180
transformed into frothing, homicidal maniacs.

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:06.210
Infusing the zombie genre with kinetic new
life, 28 Days Later proved the zombie genre

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:08.109
still had life in it yet.

00:07:08.413 --> 00:07:13.270
In the aftermath of a top-secret experiment
designed to create a global energy source,

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:18.380
a scientist named Zac Hobson awakens to find
that he is the last person alive on Earth

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:19.800
— or so he thinks.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:22.530
Soon, Hobson happens upon two other survivors.

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:27.210
As the trio discovers the common cause behind
their survival, their emerging love triangle

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:31.550
takes a backseat to Hobson's revelation that
the full extent of the experiment's pernicious

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:33.810
effects have yet to reveal themselves.

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:38.900
Overwhelmingly cryptic and appropriately lonely,
The Quiet Earth is a gorgeously photographed

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:43.528
low-budget gem grounded by three soul-wrenching
lead performances.

00:07:43.528 --> 00:07:48.750
Boasting an incredible ensemble cast and an
unsettling degree of plausibility, Contagion

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:52.840
details the arrival and fallout of an airborne
viral pandemic.

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:57.880
This film's procedural plot makes the spread
that much more compelling and terrifying.

00:07:57.880 --> 00:08:04.060
We follow the illness as it takes root, spawns
conspiracy theories, and destabilizes society.

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:08.220
Contagion makes particularly major use of
Soderbergh's talent for depicting catastrophes

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:10.520
and hyper-competence in equal measure.

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:16.349
This film was a nerve-wracking watch in 2011,
and has only become more uncanny and unsettling

00:08:16.349 --> 00:08:20.058
in the wake of the eerily similar COVID-19
pandemic.

00:08:20.442 --> 00:08:25.930
This iconic film may not initially read as
apocalyptic fiction, but brace yourself for

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:27.960
a 60-year-old spoiler.

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:33.050
When the plot's larger context is ultimately
revealed, its qualification as "end of days"

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:36.330
cinema becomes painfully, ironically obvious.

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:40.810
This film follows George Taylor, an astronaut
stranded on a strange planet dominated by

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:46.140
sentient ape-like creatures who use human
captives for sport and scientific experiments.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:51.957
"Get your stinking paws off me, you damn,
dirty ape."

00:08:51.957 --> 00:08:55.790
Still one of the bleakest films to come out
of Hollywood, Planet of the Apes features

00:08:55.790 --> 00:09:00.290
a grounded performance from Roddy McDowall
as the benevolent chimp Dr. Cornelius, and

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:04.526
closes with one of the most infamous final
shots in all of cinema.

00:09:04.938 --> 00:09:10.706
When Curtis begins to experience terrifying
hallucinations, he seeks medical help and counseling.

00:09:10.706 --> 00:09:15.230
While Curtis' work and family suffer in the
wake of his violent outbursts and horrifying

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:20.470
visions of environmental catastrophe, he can't
shake the feeling that something truly terrible

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:21.560
is on the horizon.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:26.150
Are these dreams a genuine premonition of
an incoming apocalypse ... or are they actually

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:30.010
the onset of the inherited schizophrenia he's
feared his whole life?

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:35.150
A genuinely gripping portrait of the erosive
effects of undiagnosed mental illness, Take

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:40.750
Shelter is a gripping, anxiety-riddled viewing
experience grounded by a gut-wrenching lead

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:42.598
performance from Michael Shannon.

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:47.680
Just as Harry is preparing to go on his first
date with his dream girl, he accidentally

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:52.820
receives a chilling tip-off that nuclear missiles
are going to destroy Los Angeles in less than

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:53.820
an hour.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:57.690
While Harry initially laughs off the information
as a cruel joke or the ravings of a madman,

00:09:57.690 --> 00:10:01.660
he soon learns that the threat is very real
and very imminent.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:06.740
Balancing endearingly unrelenting romantic
idealism with an undeniable sense of hopelessness,

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:12.701
this Tangerine Dream-scored neon-lit terror
trip is a love story for the end times.

00:10:13.005 --> 00:10:19.170
This genre-defying feature debut follows Byeong-gu,
an unemployed conspiracy nut who has convinced

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:24.329
himself that his former employer is an evil
alien who intends to take over the planet.

00:10:24.329 --> 00:10:28.940
As such, Byeong-gu abducts his boss and tortures
him in a subterranean dungeon.

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:35.339
As his paranoia spreads and his "alien" torture
operation grows larger and larger, the resultant

00:10:35.339 --> 00:10:38.250
chaos grows ever more intense.

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:44.550
Genre-defying and delightfully ridiculous,
there is no film quite like "Save the Green

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:48.030
Planet!" and for that fact alone, it's well
worth seeking out.

00:10:48.576 --> 00:10:54.370
Directed by the Australian auteur Peter Weir,
The Last Wave follows David Burton, a taxation

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:58.709
lawyer who is hired to act as the defense
in a murder case involving the death of an

00:10:58.709 --> 00:11:01.260
Aboriginal man during a freak rainstorm.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:06.320
When Burton begins to experience bizarre,
watery dreams, he starts to agree with the

00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:11.130
accused: The strange weather patterns are
a sign of an incoming apocalypse.

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:17.820
Ambiguous and lyrical, The Last Wave is steeped
in otherworldly strangeness as reality refuses

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:18.820
to sit still.

00:11:19.097 --> 00:11:24.019
History may remember Saul Bass for his graphic
design, but fans of apocalyptic fiction know

00:11:24.019 --> 00:11:29.719
his first and only directorial effort stands
toe-to-toe with the kinetic typography of Psycho.

00:11:29.719 --> 00:11:34.750
A pair of scientific researchers in the Arizona
desert find themselves held captive by the

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:39.760
objects of their study: A colony of ants who
have begun acting strangely in the wake of

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.090
an unprecedented cosmic event.

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:47.490
As the global implications of their ant-imposed
lockdown take hold, driving the pair to nihilism

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:53.120
and madness, humankind reveals itself to be
an outmatched and overconfident species.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:58.209
Misanthropic and enormous in its scale, "Phase
IV" takes the creature feature formula and

00:11:58.209 --> 00:12:01.759
endows it with a desperate sense of fatalism.

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:07.410
When a pair of employees at a medical supply
warehouse accidentally unleash a deadly gas,

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:10.450
the malignant vapors begin to raise the dead.

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:13.709
What's more, the warehouse's neighbors are
a cemetery and a crematorium.

00:12:13.709 --> 00:12:16.630
In short, this is a recipe for disaster.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:21.680
As the dead wrench themselves back into the
land of the living, they only have one thing

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:22.813
on their minds:

00:12:22.813 --> 00:12:26.138
"Brains."

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:30.640
One of the most confident directorial debuts
in horror history, The Return of the Living

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:35.959
Dead is a rare breed: A horror-comedy that
truly delivers on the horror, both in the

00:12:35.959 --> 00:12:40.970
gore department and in confronting the existential
probability that mankind is going to pratfall

00:12:40.970 --> 00:12:42.459
into its own destruction.

00:12:42.871 --> 00:12:48.449
A séance unleashes a horrifying glimpse of
a long-dead priest and seemingly kills the

00:12:48.449 --> 00:12:50.397
woman who experiences the vision.

00:12:50.397 --> 00:12:55.120
While other occult-leaning women attempt to
warn the powers that be of the bad vibes,

00:12:55.120 --> 00:13:00.961
the seer herself — who is very much alive
— is rescued from her grave by a passing journalist.

00:13:00.961 --> 00:13:06.208
Together, the pair digs deeper into the vision,
uncovering an imminent prophecy of undead invasion.

00:13:06.208 --> 00:13:13.100
Arguably one of the gnarliest offerings from
Italian goremaster Lucio Fulci, City of the

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:19.526
Living Dead boasts unparalleled style and
a refusal to dial down any of its apocalyptic spectacle.

00:13:19.526 --> 00:13:23.504
The final product is a miraculous and foreboding
piece of filmmaking.

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:29.279
Based on Michael Crichton's 1969 novel, The
Andromeda Strain begins with a mysterious

00:13:29.279 --> 00:13:33.589
catastrophe: The residents of a rural New
Mexico town all die after the crash landing

00:13:33.589 --> 00:13:34.709
of a satellite.

00:13:34.709 --> 00:13:39.730
The only survivors are an alcoholic man and
a screaming infant.

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:44.279
Suspecting the satellite may have brought
a vicious alien organism into Earth's atmosphere,

00:13:44.279 --> 00:13:49.680
a group of scientists conduct an investigation
in a top-secret lab armed to self-destruct

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:52.860
if any infectious agent threatens to escape.

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:57.470
Featuring science fiction harder than a diamond
with a procedural bent that will satisfy those

00:13:57.470 --> 00:14:02.970
with a love of 1970s conspiracy thrillers,
The Andromeda Strain is the cruel pinnacle

00:14:02.970 --> 00:14:04.958
of the killer virus sub-genre.

00:14:05.666 --> 00:14:10.540
Few end-of-days scenarios can contend with
the literally Earth-shattering catastrophe

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:13.804
that befell our planet roughly 66 million
years ago.

00:14:13.804 --> 00:14:18.330
Directed by Don Bluth, the former Disney artist
who dominated children's feature animation

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:23.560
during the 1980s, The Land Before Time tells
of a group of young dinosaurs who are separated

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:27.420
from their families during unprecedented environmental
shifts.

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:31.560
As they journey through the wasteland, the
group is hounded by predators and a planet

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:34.230
keen to snuff out their young lives.

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:40.050
As dire, ominous, and distressing as any of
the "adult" films on this list, The Land Before

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:45.230
Time is a masterful story of perseverance,
devastation, and the difficult necessity of

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:46.526
accepting loss.

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:52.190
Even though it's supposed to be the happiest
day of her life, Justine is absolutely miserable

00:14:52.190 --> 00:14:53.238
throughout her wedding.

00:14:53.238 --> 00:14:58.670
She's doing her best, but her severe depression
shows through the cracks, much to the embarrassment

00:14:58.670 --> 00:15:00.790
of her controlling sister, Claire.

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:05.880
Meanwhile, an immense blue planet, Melancholia,
is on a collision course with Earth.

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:12.320
As the gargantuan celestial object bears down
on our planet, Justine finds elation and peace

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:14.769
in the promise of imminent destruction.

00:15:14.769 --> 00:15:20.020
Claire, on the other hand, descends further
and further into anxiety and panic as her

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:22.160
helplessness gets the better of her.

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:27.800
Weaponizing cataclysmic destruction as a metaphor
for all-consuming depressive episodes, Melancholia

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:32.728
is a masterful, engulfing, necessarily draining
watch.

00:15:33.059 --> 00:15:37.060
The year is 2027 and humanity has become sterile.

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:41.940
As extinction looms, the planet's populace
descends into martial law and total fury.

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:46.660
We follow Theo, a former activist who is recruited
by his anti-authority ex-wife to shepherd

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:49.180
a very special woman to sanctuary.

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:55.410
No human baby has been born in nearly 20 years,
and yet somehow, this woman is pregnant.

00:15:55.410 --> 00:16:00.050
With a startlingly believable vision of dystopia
grounded in impeccably detailed production

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:05.430
design and unforgettable cinematography, Children
of Men isn't just one of the best pieces of

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:10.828
apocalyptic fiction, but one of the greatest
sci-fi films of the 21st century.

00:16:10.971 --> 00:16:16.899
Aliens have invaded Earth, and not as little
green men, but as microscopic, gelatinous

00:16:16.899 --> 00:16:21.920
spores capable of imitating and assimilating
into the populace of prospective victims.

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:26.600
Our hero is Matthew Bennell, a lab scientist
who begins to grow wise to the extraterrestrial

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:31.329
conspiracy as the signs of subversive takeover
peek through the cracks.

00:16:31.329 --> 00:16:35.709
The question is, will he be able to alert
the powers that be before it's too late?

00:16:35.709 --> 00:16:40.535
Who can he confide in when the enemy looks
like a carbon copy of the people he trusts?

00:16:40.732 --> 00:16:45.740
For our money, it's the fourth entry in the
Mad Max franchise that takes the cake… or,

00:16:45.740 --> 00:16:49.790
more accurately, the can of beans, or the
barrel of guzzolene.

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:55.649
In all honesty, there's probably no cake to
be found in this apocalypse, but Mad Max:

00:16:55.649 --> 00:16:58.550
Fury Road is a cut above its predecessors.

00:16:58.550 --> 00:17:03.180
A feature-length car chase led by a rebellious
Imperator attempting to shepherd a warlord's

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:09.300
brides to a safe haven, this film is a kinetic
rock opera of dust clouds, skull-embedded

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:11.230
wheels, and dogged perseverance.

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:17.760
A modern classic with a wasteland we are keen
to revisit time and time again, Mad Max: Fury

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:22.537
Road is the shiny, chromatic star of modern
apocalyptic cinema.

00:17:22.814 --> 00:17:25.980
"They're coming to get you, Barbara!"

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:30.769
For reasons unknown — though radiation from
a disintegrating space probe may be to blame

00:17:30.769 --> 00:17:32.940
— the dead are rising from their graves.

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:37.590
A group of survivors fleeing the rotting hordes
find themselves under one roof, where they're

00:17:37.590 --> 00:17:42.350
forced to steady their fragile nerves and
work together to keep the flesh-hungry ghouls

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:43.430
at bay.

00:17:43.430 --> 00:17:48.270
A groundbreaking, precedent-setting contribution
to the apocalyptic genre, Night of the Living

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:53.530
Dead set the stage for a litany of zombie
films keenly interested in the human response

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:55.020
to the end of days.

00:17:55.020 --> 00:18:02.400
Even more than 50 years past its initial release,
Night of the Living Dead refuses to show its age.

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:08.330
The stir-crazy residents of an Antarctic research
station find themselves in a Lovecraftian

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:14.627
nightmare when the dog they rescued explodes
into a fleshy mass of spider legs and bullwhip tentacles.

00:18:14.627 --> 00:18:20.660
This high-stakes murder mystery is less of
a whodunit than a whoisit, which unfolds as

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:26.010
the men are preyed upon by an intergalactic
creature capable of imitating organic life.

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:31.460
The gem in the crown of John Carpenter's "Apocalypse
Trilogy" — which also contains the exceptional

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:37.360
"Prince of Darkness" and "In the Mouth of
Madness" — "The Thing" is a dread-drenched epic.

00:18:37.476 --> 00:18:43.120
This is the way the world ends: Not with a
bang, but with miscommunication and politicians

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:44.549
fighting in the war room.

00:18:44.549 --> 00:18:46.799
However, there is also a bang for good measure.

00:18:46.799 --> 00:18:51.950
Simultaneously one of the scariest and funniest
films ever made, Stanley Kubrick's satirical

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:57.429
masterpiece focuses on a gaggle of politicians,
generals, and diplomats attempting to thwart

00:18:57.429 --> 00:19:02.974
an unintended nuclear holocaust instigated
by an American general maddened by conspiracy theories.

00:19:02.974 --> 00:19:09.520
Horrifyingly plausible and undeniably hilarious,
Dr. Strangelove is a classic for a reason.

00:19:10.362 --> 00:19:15.440
A guide, known as a "stalker" in the film,
shepherds two curious men through a bizarre

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:18.150
area known as "the Zone."

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:25.972
Mysterious and forbidden, the Zone is a physics-defying
land at the epicenter of an unspeakable extraterrestrial tragedy.

00:19:25.972 --> 00:19:31.870
In the core of the Zone lies their destination:
The Room, a mystical space that seems to grant

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:35.730
the deepest, darkest wishes of all who enter
it.

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:41.370
Directed by the great Soviet filmmaker Andrei
Tarkovsky, "Stalker" is an evasive, yet evocative,

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:44.120
take on science fiction's deepest questions.

